---
/**
 * A short pitch for the translation itself — credential, not seminar.
 * The full case lives at litbible.net/translation-commitments.
 */
---

<section class="about">
  <div class="container about__inner">
    <h2 class="about__title">About the Translation</h2>
    <p class="about__lede">
      The Liberation &amp; Inclusion Translation is an independent, scholar-driven
      rendering of the New Testament, faithful to the Greek, and unwilling to
      launder the harm the text has been used to justify. It reads from the
      vantage of the people it was first written to: the poor, the grieving,
      the pushed-aside.
    </p>
    <p class="about__more">
      <a href="/translation-commitments/">
        Read the Translation Commitments →
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-7);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about {
      padding-block: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
  .about__inner {
    max-width: var(--measure-prose);
  }
  .about__title {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .about__lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  .about__more {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
  .about__more a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
